   Below we implement the same result in two phases, in an order that
   improves data locality and enables vectorization and (column-wise)
   parallelization:

     1) ACCUM: B[i, j] += sum_{k=i+1..M-1} A[k, i] * B[k, j]
     2) SCALE: B[i, j] *= alpha

   This is algebraically identical to the original kernel and preserves
   the in-place semantics (no extra matrices are allocated).
*/
static
void kernel_trmm[[gnu::flatten, gnu::noinline]](int m, int n,
		 DATA_TYPE alpha,
		 DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(A,M,M,m,m),
		 DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(B,M,N,m,n))
{
